From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] main menu: the Long Way Home line, and a menu that finishes opening

Gate G1 and the first half of G2 (docs/the-entry-point.md): the game has no way in from its menus,
and this is the one attach point the main menu needs. The line itself -- the button, its callback,
and the start-state selector it opens -- lives in module/ui/ui_lwh_start.cpp and is compiled in from
LWH_MODULE_DIR like every other piece of our logic. This patch only calls it.

`LWH_UI_MainMenuAdd` is called after the eight retail buttons are added, so the new item is the
menu's last and renders in the retail grid's one free cell. With LWH_UI unset the call and its
inline no-op collapse to nothing and the menu is exactly upstream's, which is what keeps mode 1
unmodified in behaviour.

The second hunk is a robustness fix that a menu with an added line forces into the open: the opening
animation ended only on a frame where its per-frame counter was exactly buttonCnt-1 (7). At a low
frame rate one frame can step the counter from 6 to 8 and skip 7, and the menu then sits in its
opening animation forever -- the buttons are never drawn, so any line added to them never appears.
`>=` completes the opening on the frame it reaches the last-but-one button, which is what the
normal case does; the only behaviour it changes is the hang.

diff --git a/efgame/src/ui/ui_menu.cpp b/efgame/src/ui/ui_menu.cpp
index 169d942..91e9911 100755
--- a/efgame/src/ui/ui_menu.cpp
+++ b/efgame/src/ui/ui_menu.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,11 @@
 #include "ui_local.h"
+#include "lwh_ui_hooks.h"
+
+#ifndef LWH_UI
+// Without our UI module (LWH_UI unset) the main menu is exactly upstream's: the attach point below
+// compiles to nothing. With it set, lwh_ui.h declares the real one.
+inline void LWH_UI_MainMenuAdd( void * ) {}
+#endif
 
 void UI_VirtualSaveMenu(int from);
 
@@ -2823,7 +2830,12 @@ void M_Main_Opening (void)
 
 		ui.R_SetColor( NULL );
 
-		if (iMax == (buttonCnt - 1))	// End of menu opening
+		// End of menu opening. `>=` and not `==`: at a low frame rate a single frame can step
+		// iMax from 6 to 8 and skip 7, and `== 7` then never fires -- the menu sits in its opening
+		// animation forever and the buttons (and any line added to them) are never drawn. With
+		// `>=` the opening completes on the first frame it reaches the last-but-one button, which
+		// is what the normal case does; it changes nothing except that the hang cannot happen.
+		if (iMax >= (buttonCnt - 1))	// End of menu opening
 		{
 			iMaxHold = 0;
 
@@ -3633,6 +3645,10 @@ void MainMenu_Init( void )
 	Menu_AddItem( &s_main_menu,	&s_wormhole_label );
 	Menu_AddItem( &s_main_menu,	&s_core_label );
 
+	// Long Way Home: the third mode's own line, beside the retail ones (docs/client-modes.md). The
+	// line itself is ours (module/ui/ui_lwh_start.cpp); this is only the attach point.
+	LWH_UI_MainMenuAdd( &s_main_menu );
+
 	s_main_menu.initialized = qtrue;
 
 
